<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Amyntas of Galatia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 25 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a> · Also known as Amyntas of Galatia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Amyntas was the last king of Galatia in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>, ruling from 36 to 25 BCE. A former secretary of the Galatian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deiotarus">Deiotarus</a>, he was made king by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mark-antony">Mark Antony</a>, went over to Octavian before Actium, and extended his rule over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pisidia">Pisidia</a>, Lycaonia and parts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cilicia">Cilicia</a>. He was killed fighting the Homonadenses of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taurus-mountains">Taurus</a> mountains, and Augustus made his kingdom the Roman province of Galatia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/amyntas-of-galatia.jpg" alt="Amyntas of Galatia" width="320" height="141" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Amyntas_of_Galatia.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
